// ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
// ┃  ZMK Corne Configuration                 ┃
// ┣━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┫
// ┃  ajpemok                                 ┃
// ┃  Corne 42 Key Layout                     ┃
// ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛

#include <behaviors.dtsi>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/bt.h>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/keys.h>
#include <dt-bindings/zmk/outputs.h>

// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  Hold-Tap Configuration Guide            ║
// ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
// ║  detailed explanation of all timing      ║
// ║  and resolution variables                ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
// ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │  This section defines exactly how ZMK    │
// │  resolves dual-function behaviours.      │
// │                                          │
// │  Timers (Milliseconds):                  │
// │  - tapping-term-ms: The primary timer.   │
// │    Releasing before this sends a tap.    │
// │  - quick-tap-ms: The double-tap window.  │
// │    Tapping again within this repeats     │
// │    the tap instead of holding.           │
// │  - require-prior-idle-ms: The typing     │
// │    buffer to prevent accidental holds.   │
// │                                          │
// │  Flavours (Resolution Strategy):         │
// │  - hold-preferred: The instant another   │
// │    key is pressed, it becomes a hold.    │
// │  - tap-preferred: Prioritises typing.    │
// │    It stays a tap if released early.     │
// │  - balanced: The home-row sweet spot.    │
// │    It becomes a hold if another key is   │
// │    pressed AND released while held.      │
// │  - tap-unless-interrupted: Resolves as   │
// │    a tap unless another key is pressed   │
// │    and released during the hold window.  │
// │                                          │
// │  Advanced Modifiers:                     │
// │  - hold-while-undecided: Sends the hold  │
// │    keycode to the OS immediately while   │
// │    ZMK decides if it is a tap or hold.   │
// │  - hold-while-undecided-linger: Keeps    │
// │    the hold active briefly to ensure     │
// │    the OS registers the modifier.        │
// │  - retro-tap: Sends the tap action if    │
// │    held past the term but released       │
// │    without pressing any other keys.      │
// │  - hold-trigger-key-positions: Cross     │
// │    hand blocking to restrict modifiers   │
// │    to opposite-hand key presses.         │
// │  - hold-trigger-on-release: Pauses the   │
// │    flavour logic until you let go of     │
// │    the key.                              │
// └──────────────────────────────────────────┘

/ {
    behaviors {
        // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
        // ║  1. Core Typing (Home Row Mods)          ║
        // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
        // ║  hand-blocked modifiers for the          ║
        // ║  primary alpha keys                      ║
        // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
        // › use case: primary alpha keys on the left hand, blocks same-hand modifier activation

        mt_home_row_mod_left: home_row_mod_left {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "HOME_ROW_MOD_LEFT";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <175>;
            quick-tap-ms = <150>;
            require-prior-idle-ms = <150>;
            flavor = "balanced";
            hold-trigger-key-positions = <6 18 30 40 39 41 35 23 11 10 18 19 20 21 22 30 31 32 33 34 7 8 9>;
            hold-trigger-on-release;
        };

        // › use case: primary alpha keys on the right hand, faster timings for right-hand dominance

        mt_home_row_mod_right: home_row_mod_right {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "HOME_ROW_MOD_RIGHT";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <150>;
            quick-tap-ms = <125>;
            require-prior-idle-ms = <100>;
            flavor = "balanced";
            hold-trigger-on-release;
            hold-trigger-key-positions = <0 1 2 3 4 5 12 13 14 15 16 17 24 25 26 27 28 29 36 37 38>;
        };

        // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
        // ║  2. Layer Taps (CLT)                     ║
        // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
        // ║  variants for momentary layer shifts     ║
        // ║  using <&mo>, <&kp> bindings             ║
        // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
        // › use case: fast typing standard, prioritises clean typing over accidental layer shifts

        clt_tap_pref: layer_tap_preferred {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "LAYER_TAP_PREFERRED";
            bindings = <&mo>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            flavor = "tap-preferred";
            tapping-term-ms = <150>;
            quick-tap-ms = <125>;
        };

        // › use case: standard balanced thumb layer toggle for smooth rolling motions

        clt_balanced: layer_tap_balanced {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "LAYER_TAP_BALANCED";
            bindings = <&mo>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            flavor = "balanced";
            tapping-term-ms = <200>;
            quick-tap-ms = <150>;
        };

        // › use case: highly deliberate layer shift for settings or dangerous macros to prevent misfires

        clt_deliberate: layer_tap_deliberate {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "LAYER_TAP_DELIBERATE";
            bindings = <&mo>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            flavor = "tap-preferred";
            tapping-term-ms = <300>;
            quick-tap-ms = <150>;
        };

        // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
        // ║  3. Mod Taps (CMT)                       ║
        // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
        // ║  variants for custom modifiers           ║
        // ║  using <&kp>, <&kp> bindings             ║
        // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
        // › use case: standard thumb modifier requiring stability during fast rolling motions

        cmt_balanced: mod_tap_balanced {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "MOD_TAP_BALANCED";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <200>;
            quick-tap-ms = <150>;
            require-prior-idle-ms = <150>;
            flavor = "balanced";
        };

        // › use case: aggressive speed typists needing to prevent accidental mods during overlapping rolls

        cmt_tui: mod_tap_tui {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "MOD_TAP_TUI";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <200>;
            quick-tap-ms = <150>;
            require-prior-idle-ms = <150>;
            flavor = "tap-unless-interrupted";
        };

        // › use case: ideal for keys you might accidentally linger on but still expect a tap output

        cmt_retro: mod_tap_retro {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "MOD_TAP_RETRO";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <150>;
            retro-tap;
            quick-tap-ms = <125>;
            flavor = "tap-preferred";
        };

        // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
        // ║  4. Tap-Dances                           ║
        // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
        // ║  multi-tap triggers for complex          ║
        // ║  modifiers and locks                     ║
        // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
        // › use case: single tap sends Hyper (Cmd+Ctrl+Alt+Shift), double tap sends Meh

        td_hyper_meh: dance_hyper_meh {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-tap-dance";
            label = "DANCE_HYPER_MEH";
            #binding-cells = <0>;
            bindings = <&kp LA(LC(LG(LSHFT)))>, <&kp LA(LC(LSHFT))>;

            tapping-term-ms = <175>;
        };

        // › use case: single tap sends Meh (Ctrl+Alt+Shift), double tap sends Hyper

        td_meh_hyper: dance_meh_hyper {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-tap-dance";
            label = "DANCE_MEH_HYPER";
            #binding-cells = <0>;
            bindings = <&kp LA(LC(LSHFT))>, <&kp LA(LC(LG(LSHFT)))>;

            tapping-term-ms = <175>;
        };

        // › use case: single tap toggles Caps Word (auto-disables on non-alphanumeric keys like space or enter), double tap locks Caps Lock

        td_caps_word: dance_caps_word {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-tap-dance";
            label = "DANCE_CAPS_WORD";
            #binding-cells = <0>;
            tapping-term-ms = <200>;
            bindings = <&caps_word>, <&kp CAPSLOCK>;
        };

        // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗
        // ║  5. Mod-Morphs                           ║
        // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════╣
        // ║  context-aware keys for symbols and      ║
        // ║  navigation utility                      ║
        // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝
        // › use case: tap for Escape, Shift+tap for Grave/Tilde

        mm_esc_grave: morph_esc_grave {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-mod-morph";
            label = "MORPH_ESC_GRAVE";
            bindings = <&kp ESC>, <&kp GRAVE>;

            #binding-cells = <0>;
            mods = <(MOD_LSFT|MOD_RSFT)>;
        };

        // › use case: tap for Backspace, Shift+tap for Delete

        mm_bspc_del: morph_bspc_del {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-mod-morph";
            label = "MORPH_BSPC_DEL";
            bindings = <&kp BACKSPACE>, <&kp DEL>;

            #binding-cells = <0>;
            mods = <(MOD_LSFT|MOD_RSFT)>;
        };

        // › use case: tap for Left Parenthesis, Shift+tap for Exclamation mark

        mm_l_paren: morph_l_paren {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-mod-morph";
            label = "MORPH_L_PAREN";
            bindings = <&kp LEFT_PARENTHESIS>, <&kp EXCLAMATION>;

            #binding-cells = <0>;
            mods = <(MOD_LSFT|MOD_RSFT)>;
        };

        // › use case: tap for Right Parenthesis, Shift+tap for Exclamation mark

        mm_r_paren: morph_r_paren {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-mod-morph";
            label = "MORPH_R_PAREN";
            bindings = <&kp RIGHT_PARENTHESIS>, <&kp PIPE>;

            #binding-cells = <0>;
            mods = <(MOD_LSFT|MOD_RSFT)>;
        };
    };

    combos {
        compatible = "zmk,combos";

        combo_jk_backspace {
            bindings = <&kp DEL>;
            key-positions = <19 20>;
        };
    };

    keymap {
        compatible = "zmk,keymap";

        main {
            label = "main";
            bindings = <
&mm_esc_grave        &kp Q                             &kp W                             &kp E                          &kp R                          &kp T                    &kp Y      &kp U                                 &kp I                           &kp O                               &kp P                                       &kp MINUS
&kp TAB              &mt_home_row_mod_left LEFT_GUI A  &mt_home_row_mod_left LEFT_ALT S  &mt_home_row_mod_left LCTRL D  &mt_home_row_mod_left LSHFT F  &kp G                    &kp H      &mt_home_row_mod_right RIGHT_SHIFT J  &mt_home_row_mod_right RCTRL K  &mt_home_row_mod_right RIGHT_ALT L  &mt_home_row_mod_right RIGHT_GUI SEMICOLON  &kp SQT
&clt_balanced 1 F24  &kp Z                             &kp X                             &kp C                          &kp V                          &kp B                    &kp N      &kp M                                 &kp COMMA                       &kp DOT                             &kp SLASH                                   &kp ENTER
                                                                                         &td_meh_hyper                  &td_hyper_meh                  &clt_tap_pref 2 SPACE    &kp ENTER  &clt_balanced 1 BACKSPACE             &clt_balanced 2 DELETE
            >;
        };

        movement {
            label = "movement";
            bindings = <
&kp GRAVE  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &kp HOME  &kp PAGE_DOWN  &kp PAGE_UP  &kp END    &trans  &trans
&trans     &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &kp LEFT  &kp DOWN       &kp UP       &kp RIGHT  &trans  &trans
&trans     &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &trans    &trans         &trans       &trans     &trans  &trans
                           &trans  &trans  &trans    &trans    &trans         &trans
            >;
        };

        number {
            label = "number";
            bindings = <
&trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &kp N7  &kp N8  &kp N9              &kp ASTRK  &kp LBKT        &kp RBKT
&trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &kp N4  &kp N5  &kp N6              &kp MINUS  &mm_l_paren     &mm_r_paren
&trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans    &kp N1  &kp N2  &kp N3              &kp PLUS   &kp FSLH        &kp BSLH
                        &trans  &trans  &trans    &trans  &kp N0  &mt RSHFT KP_EQUAL
            >;
        };

        transition {
            label = "transition";
            bindings = <
&kp F1   &kp F2   &kp F3   &kp F4   &kp F5   &kp F6     &kp F7   &kp F8   &kp F9   &kp F10  &kp F11  &kp F12
&kp F13  &kp F14  &kp F15  &kp F16  &kp F17  &kp F18    &kp F19  &kp F20  &kp F21  &kp F22  &kp F23  &kp F24
&trans   &trans   &trans   &trans   &trans   &sl 4      &trans   &trans   &trans   &trans   &trans   &trans
                           &trans   &trans   &trans     &trans   &trans   &trans
            >;
        };

        io {
            label = "io";
            bindings = <
&trans  &bt BT_DISC 0  &bt BT_DISC 1  &bt BT_DISC 2  &bt BT_DISC 3  &bt BT_DISC 4    &out OUT_TOG  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &bt BT_CLR
&trans  &bt BT_SEL 0   &bt BT_SEL 1   &bt BT_SEL 2   &bt BT_SEL 3   &bt BT_SEL 4     &trans        &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans
&trans  &trans         &trans         &trans         &trans         &trans           &trans        &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans  &trans
                                      &trans         &trans         &trans           &trans        &trans  &trans
            >;
        };
    };

    conditional_layers {
        compatible = "zmk,conditional-layers";

        tri_layer {
            if-layers = <1 2>;
            then-layer = <3>;
        };
    };
};
